# New night-canoe scene — preview assets

Source: the user's `Night journey through the mangroves.png`, preserved in `../scene-references/downloads-2026-10-11/`.

This set retains the new scene's diagonal canoe formation, character designs, costumes and seating. It supplies eight full-canvas transparent fleet cels, a clean 4:3 background and a separate foreground root layer. The foreground roots were removed from the background before being composited in front of the boats.

All selected art was generated with built-in imagegen. Exact prompts are in `prompts.json`. The brighter discarded release variant was not selected. Cels use a common 1672×941 registration canvas and uniform aspect-preserving scaling.

The preview uses the existing episode renderer and the approved 48-frame exposure cycle twice, for 96 output frames / four seconds at 24 fps. The camera, boat travel, heave, water and foreground move on separate tracks. This is a silent motion preview with held passenger acting and generated paddling cels; the full 12-second source shot is not marked complete.

From `episode-01/`:

```bash
python render_new_scene_preview.py --output build/new-night-scene-new-take
```

Settings: `data/new-night-scene-preview.json`. Output: `build/new-night-scene-take-01/animation.mp4` and its `index.html` player. Existing approved takes remain intact.
